EVIDENCE ICON-SETS

INSTALLATION

  evidence icon-sets go in a directory below $PREFIX/share/evidence/icons;
  if the default prefix /usr/local is used, the "tosh" theme (128x128 pixels)
  would hence be expected in a folder /usr/local/share/evidence/icons/tosh_128

  If you got evidence from CVS, the icons will be generated and installed
  as part of the normal ./configure, make, checkinstall cycle.

USE

  If the --iconset command-line option is not given, evidence will try to
  load the iconset suggested by the active theme.  If no such suggestion was
  made, evidence will try find an iconset called "default" -- usually a symlink
  to one of the supplied sets.  Failing that, shelf and icon-view will be
  disabled.

TERMS OF USE

  Every iconset should contain a notice on which artist kindly made them
  available, and what the conditions of use, if any, are.

DESCRIPTION

emblems

  This is a special directory containing "emblems" -- labels to go
  on top of an icon to indicate "read-only" state and similar things.
  Icon-themes can reference these default emblems if they don't bring
  their own.

ento_48/ento_64

  Various insects and arachnoids in the popular "aquatic" style

fishtank_48/fishtank_128

  Various fish, for use by the fishtank theme

gfilerunner

  Default iconset for GNOME 1 (presumably)

gorilla_36/gorilla_48/gorilla_72

  Iconset used by the Nautilus file-manager, rendered from SVG to PNG

icosx

  OS X-like icons; mapping provided by Andrew Elcock.

efm

  Original efm icons (with some quick hacks on gfilerunner icons added
  for good measure).

tosh

  Original evidence icons by Azundris.
